2 CONT 	1.  Captain Hernando de Villegas, settled in Lagos and married to Inés López de Nava y López Muñiz on 8 Sep 1588.
2 CONT 	2.  Pedro Calderón, one of León's founding settlers in 1576.  Died there celibate in 1610 and made a will.
2 CONT 	3.  Teresa de Rodas married Benito Martín, founder of Irapuato.  A daughter, Teresa de Rodas wed Francisco Martín Gallardo (a son of Juan Rodríguez Galán and Leonor Martín).  Their son, Nicolás Gallardo married Juana Rincó
2 CONC n de Ortega.
2 CONT 	4.  Isabel de Rodas wed Francisco Covarrubias, a Familiar del Santo Oficio de la Inquisición in Zacatecas.  A daughter, Isabel de Rodas married Captain Jacinto de Talamantes, neighbors of Zacatecas.  Their male children used the
2 CONC  surname Covarrubias, and I believe that the persons with this surname descend from them in part.  A daughter, Isabel de Talamantes, wed José de Haro, from Tlaltenango and they moved to Parral, Chihuahua.
2 CONT 	The dispensa illustrates how the Covarrubias surname was perpetuated by the seed of the Talamantes-Covarrubias marriages:
2 CONT 	(6111) Tlaltenango, 28 Apr 1747.  A fourth degree of consanguinity between Antonio Benito Covarrubias, 23, from Monte de Atolinga, h.l. Agustín Covarrubias and María Pérez de Tejeda, deceased, and Rosalía Raygosa, 18, h.l. Ma
2 CONC rcos Raygosa, deceased and Ana de Santiago Mojarro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacinto Talamantes-Ysabel Covarrubias
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Lucas Covarrubias----------------------	1----------------	Pedro Covarrubias
2 CONT 	Melchora Covarrubias------------------	2----------------	Antonio Covarrubias
2 CONT 	Marcos Raygosa-------------------------	3----------------	Agustín Covarrubias
2 CONT 	la pretensa--------------------------------	4----------------	el pretenso
2 CONT
2 CONT Magdalena gave birth to four children and died in the labor of Francisco, before he was christened on 21 May 1646.  He became a priest and used the name Francisco de Orozco Agüero.  I have his clerical record.  Two daughters marr
2 CONC ied.
2 CONT 	It was likely that while a widower, Francisco de Orozco begat a natural daughter in Teocaltiche, Angela de Orozco (who wed Juan Pérez Gallo), the mother being Catalina de Arriola e Ibarra.  Have "dispensas matrimoniales" that po
2 CONC int to this illegitimate daughter.  One of the notary records brought back from Aguascalientes is the will of Franciso's sister Ana de Orozco, dated 1 Nov 1670.  She was a spinster.  She named her brother's natural daughter in the
2 CONC  will and bequeathed that 50 pesos be given to the niece.  The mother connects with one of your direct lines, the Ibarras.
2 CONT 	Francisco de Orozco's second matrimony on 15 Aug 1650 was in León, with Inés de Villegas, from Lagos, christened 16 Jan 1628.  Her parents were Hernando de Villegas y López de Nava and María Ortiz de Parada.  Because they mar
2 CONC ried outside their parish without permission, the couple was separated eight years later and the oldest litigation I've found to date in "dispensas" ensued.  It's in reel 10260 AGN-began 28 Sep 1658 and carried over to 1659.  Fran
2 CONC cisco testified that second year and said he was age 45, born in Aguascalientes, so his birth year was about 1614 (1659-45).
2 CONT 	The only daughter found for this, his second wedlock, was Catalina de Orozco, baptized in Lagos 20 Jan 1652, who there married on 4 Nov 1666 to Lorenzo de Carbajal, a son of Rodrigo de Carbajal y Ulloa and Juana de Lomelín y Ben
2 CONC avides, from Nochistlán.
