2 CONT Your Huerta ancestor, Captain Juan, married twice and your line proceeds from the second spouse, María de Quijas y Escalante.  The twice married factor, however, and thus the identification of your Juan's parents, was missing fro
2 CONC m the Family Group Sheet.  While it had been in my notes about the Teocaltiche "capellanía" (film 6872, Capellanías, AGN).  Better late than never.
2 CONT 	The man in question was born in Teocaltiche c. 1612, a son of Captain Pedro de Huerta y Sánchez and María González de Ruvalcaba y López de Fuenllana.  I believe he was the last child, though can't prove it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Gerónimo de Huerta y Escalante's parents are confirmed by his mother's will dated 5 December 1698, with a "codicilio" of 11 December.  Made in Aguascalientes before the Juez Rector Alonso Ruiz de Escamilla in the absence 
2 CONC of Pedro Antonio Gallardo, Alcalde Ordinario, the original document is at the Archivo Histórico del Estado de Aguascalientes that houses the notary records.  It's in Caja 3, Expediente 5, Escritura 23, Fojas 31 frente-36 vuelta. 
2 CONC  A summary forthwith:
2 CONT 	"yo, Doña María de Quijas Escalante viuda del Capitán Juan de Huerta vecino que fue de la Villa de Aguascalientes, hija lexitima del Capitán Pedro de Quijas y de Catalina de Saldañavecinos que fueron de la jurisdicción de S
2 CONC ierra de Pinos y yo vecina de dicha villa..."
2 CONT 	She stated that her burial should be in the convent of San Diego in Aguascalientes.  Her husband, defunct 32 years before, has his burial entry 1 February 1666 and was probably interred there.  That record says he made his will i
