2 CONC a y Escalante and his spouse, with her parents identified by these two records.  Rosa María changed her mind about whom she'd marry (or her father did) with only 10 days difference.  Must have been the reason why the Corregidor, 
2 CONC who got wind of the fact that she'd given another the promise to marry, was against the marriage to Marentes Otaduí y Avendaño (whom she did marry).
2 CONT 	The composite surname of Captain Gerónimo's spouse in these two entries is eloquent.  In three of the baptisms of her daughters, she's named Juana Flores; Juana Rentería y Flores in the fourth, and Juana Flores Alatorre in the 
2 CONC records of the capellanía founded in Teocaltiche in 1622.
