1 NOTE 2.  The Morelia dispensa on 21 January 1684 for widower Diego Ochoa Garibay and María Barroso de Ruvalcaba.  Born 5 July 1661 in Hacienda de las Mesillas, she was christened in Lagos 29 September 1661.  I didn't have her married.
2 CONC   Parents: Captain Juan González de Ruvalcaba (a son of Capt. Fulgencio González de Ruvalcaba y López de Fuenllana and Luisa de Rodas), and Catalina Díaz Barroso.  Her parents, not known to me.  The family moved to their hacie
2 CONC nda near Silao between the above christening date and 26 November 1665, date of the Silao christening of daughter Francisca (married to Juan Bartolomé Fernández de Souza y Acevedo).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.	Born in Aguascalientes c. 1608, Jacinto Lozano's marriage took place c. 1632 in Lagos de Moreno, Jalisco.  The bride: Juana González de Ruvalcaba, there born to Captain Fulgencio González de Ruvalcaba and Luisa de Rodas.  Jua
2 CONC na died in Aguascalientes, June 1651 in the birth of their tenth child.  Jacinto remarried in Juchipila, Zacatecas to Ana de Lara; no offspring.  Descendants from first spouse found in Aguascalientes, Ags.; Juchipila and Nochistla
2 CONC ́n, Zacatecas; Teocaltiche, Jalisco and the latter state's "Los Altos" area.
2 CONT
