1 NOTE In his first wedlock, Juan was not mentioned as a Captain in the records I've seen.  The marital vows were c. 1642, probably in Lagos, the place of origin of the bride, María de Nava (sometimes named María Macías-ostensibly a m
2 CONC ember of the Macías Valadés family).  Have not succeeded in identifying her parents.  They lived in Lagos until late 1648 and moved to Jalostotitlán before the 1650 Census, where both and three heirs appear registered.
2 CONT 	Four known children:
2 CONT 	1. Licenciado Juan de Huerta, christened in Lagos 17 Feb 1643 (listed as age 7 in the 1650 Jalos Census).  He was a priest and the second "capellán" as of 16 May 1662.  Substituted his uncle, Bachiller Alonso Muñoz de Huerta, w
2 CONC ho was the priest of San Juan de los Lagos until he died there in November of 1659.  Passed away before 5 Sep 1710.
2 CONT 	2. In Lagos, 26 Mar 1645 was the christening of Pedro de Huerta y Nava, listed at age 5 in the 1650 Census.  His wife was Leonor de Hermosillo y Córdova, born in Jalos in 1646 (age 4 in 1650), whose parents were Jerónimo Camach
2 CONC o y Hermosillo and Catalina González Rubio y Torres.  Pedro was the "Regidor" in Guadalajara.  Know of a son and a daughter who married.
2 CONT 	3. Catalina de Huerta, christened in ibid. 12 Sep 1646 (age 3 in 1650).  No longer appears.
2 CONT 	4. María, who died a young child because she is not in the 1650 Census, was christened in Lagos on 29 Nov 1648.
2 CONT 	The first wife died after the 1650 Census and estimated before 1656.  Some time in between, Juan took his second wife, María de Quijas y Escalante.  It might have occurred in Guadalajara (refer to his death entry in 1666) and th
2 CONC e first offspring may have been born there.  They certainly did not remain in "los Altos" and are not in Aguascalientes yet.  Known children:
