2 CONT Baptism of his daughter Beatrice , "Mexico, Aguascalientes, Parish Records, 1601-1962," FamilySearch Image Database ( https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:S3HY-6QQ9-YQ7?cc=  6 October 2022), Aguascalientes > Assumption of Mary 
2 CONC > Baptisms 1616-1662 > image 81 of 334 ; Catholic parishes, Aguascalientes.
2 CONT Testament of his son-in-law Pedro Romo de Vivar
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Wedding [1]
2 CONT In the stay of Morcenique [on] sixteen days of the month of May of [1]623 years, I married [and veiled] premises the solemnities of right to Luis Tiscareño de Molina , son of Juan Tiscareño and Elvira Márquez, natives of Triana in
2 CONC  Seville [in the] Kingdoms of Castile, with Lorença Ruiz de Esparça, legitimate daughter of Lope Ruiz de Esparça and Francisca Gabadi, his wife, neighbors of this town [Aguascalientes], witnesses were Martín Fernández de Vaulus an
2 CONC d Francisco Macías Valades, Salvador Ruiz de Esparça, brother-in-law of the said Luis Tiscareno de Molina, godparents were Francisco Sánchez de Montes de Oca and Ana Ruiz de Esparça, his wife, brothers-in-law of the said Luis Tisc
2 CONC areño, and I signed it as a testimony of truth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lorenzo de la Vera
2 CONT
2 CONT Death [2]
2 CONT On February 20, 1660, I buried Luis de Tiscareño , a Spaniard, the husband of Lorensa Ruiz de Esparza. He confessed and received the viaticum, not testo, nor did he receive the holy oil because it is understood that it was not his
2 CONC  risk ailment. And I signed it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Bartolomé de Soto y Carvajal
2 CONT
2 CONT Fuentes
