1 NOTE 12. The Lagos wedding of 18 Feb 1635 was between Magdalena Gómez Portugal and Francisco de Orozco, "vecino de Aguascalientes."  Her parents and the "padrinos" are included: "Diego Gómez y María de Arrona; Don Alonso de Castro y
2 CONC  Doña María Altamirano su mujer, vecinos desta."  From other records, the husband was a son of Gerónimo Orozco and Angela de Velasco.  Both of his parents and their ancestries are in the Archdeacon's writings because Gerónimo 
2 CONC de Orozco (misnamed Francisco, while his brother, Francisco de Orozco is misnamed Gerónimo) descended from "Alberto de Orozco, primo hermano del señor Presidente Orozco."  Dr. Gerónimo de Orozco y Lerma, Gobernador y Capitán G
2 CONC eneral de la Nueva Galicia.  Angela de Velasco descended from the Flores de la Torre lineage.  Her parents were Juan Ramírez de la Campaña (misnamed Cristóbal in the manuscript) and Francisca Temiño de Velasco, and her parents
2 CONC  were Captain Diego Flores de la Torre and Angela Velasco.
2 CONT 	The 1635 wedding above was on the same date as the second marriage of Angelina (No.5) to Pedro de Cuéllar.
2 CONT 	Magdalena gave birth to four children and died in the labor of Francisco, before he was christened on 21 May 1646.  He became a priest and used the name Francisco de Orozco Agüero.  I have his clerical record.  Two daughters mar
2 CONC ried.
2 CONT 	It was likely that while a widower, Francisco de Orozco begat a natural daughter in Teocaltiche, Angela de Orozco (who wed Juan Pérez Gallo), the mother being Catalina de Arriola e Ibarra.  Have "dispensas matrimoniales" that po
2 CONC int to this illegitimate daughter.  One of the notary records brought back from Aguascalientes is the will of Franciso's sister Ana de Orozco, dated 1 Nov 1670.  She was a spinster.  She named her brother's natural daughter in the
2 CONC  will and bequeathed that 50 pesos be given to the niece.  The mother connects with one of your direct lines, the Ibarras.
2 CONT 	Francisco de Orozco's second matrimony on 15 Aug 1650 was in León, with Inés de Villegas, from Lagos, christened 16 Jan 1628.  Her parents were Hernando de Villegas y López de Nava and María Ortiz de Parada.  Because they mar
2 CONC ried outside their parish without permission, the couple was separated eight years later and the oldest litigation I've found to date in "dispensas" ensued.  It's in reel 10260 AGN-began 28 Sep 1658 and carried over to 1659.  Fran
2 CONC cisco testified that second year and said he was age 45, born in Aguascalientes, so his birth year was about 1614 (1659-45).
2 CONT 	The only daughter found for this, his second wedlock, was Catalina de Orozco, baptized in Lagos 20 Jan 1652, who there married on 4 Nov 1666 to Lorenzo de Carbajal, a son of Rodrigo de Carbajal y Ulloa and Juana de Lomelín y Ben
2 CONC avides, from Nochistlán.
2 CONT
2 CONT
