1 NAME Juan /Lozano y Zapata/
2 GIVN Juan
2 SURN Lozano y Zapata
2 _MARNM Lozano y Zapata
2 NICK Capt. Juan Lozano
2 NICK Juan Lozano (Geni Tree Match)
1 NAME Capt. Juan Lozano y Zapata
1 NAME Juan //
2 GIVN Juan
2 SURN De Lozano
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 PLAC Nueva Galicia,Nueva Espana,now Aguascalientes,Mexico
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1530
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lobon
3 STAE Badajoz
3 CTRY España
1 OCCU Capitan
1 TITL Capitán
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} " Captain Juan Lozano was born in Lobón around 1530. He was the son of Alonso Hernández Lozano, Mayor of the State of Hijosdalgo de Badajoz in the first half of the 16th century, and his wife María Zapata. Captain 
2 CONC Juan Lozano , as stated therein information, he went to New Spain in 1560," with his wife Inés Martínez, originally from Badajoz; daughter of Francisco Martínez Vaca and Isabel González, natives and neighbors of Badajoz, Hijosdalg
2 CONC o." [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT " Captain Juan Lozano and his wife Inés Martínez went to New Spain - as has already been said - in 1560, and the genearch had the character of Caudillo of the Presidio of Sombrerete." In 1611 he was a resident of Guadalajara. Capt
2 CONC ain Juan Lozano and his wife Inés Martínez were parents of: a) Cristóbal Martín Lozano, also known as Cristóbal Martínez Lozano, who has traditionally been noted as one of the founders of the Villa de Nuestra Señora de la Asunción
2 CONC  de Aguascalientes in 1575 " [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT ↑ Offshoots of Spain in New Galicia: v. 1. Genealogical dictionary of the Alteña families (Gutiérrez-Hurtado de Mendoza), Volume 5, Part 2 of Retoños de España in Nueva Galicia, Jalisco (Mexico). General Secretariat of Government,
2 CONC  Mariano González-Leal, Government of Jalisco, General Secretariat of Government, Directorate of Publications, 2011, University of California
