2 CONT * 1047. GENEALOGIA DE NOTCHISTLAN ANTIGUO REINO DE LA NUEVA GALICIA EN EL SIGLO XVII SEGUN SUS ARCHIVOS PARROQUIALES
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * [http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/MEX-JALISCO/2002-09/1033184653 Jalisco: Robalcaba / Ruvalcaba / Robalcava]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Rubalcaba's Come to Nueva Galicia
2 CONT
2 CONT The first known Rubalcava to arrive in the area of Nueva Galicia (Jalisco, Zacatecas and Aguascalientes) was Matheo González de Rubalcava, who was allegedly a native of Liérganes, Santander, born sometime around 1490. His wife was
2 CONC  Juana María Gonzalez, the daughter of the conquistador, Ruy Gonzalez. One of his sons was Capitán Alonso Gonzalez de Ruvalcaba, who eventually moved to Teocaltiche (located in present-day Jalisco, just south of the State of Aguas
2 CONC calientes and each of Nochistlán in Zacatecas) and is the ancestor of many Rubalcava's in that area.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is believed that the surname González de Rubalcava implies "the González family from the place called Rubalcava." However, after a few generations in Mexico, most descendants discarded the Gonzalez but retained Rubalcava or som
2 CONC e variant of it.
