2 CONT .  I obtained their marriage in Sierra de Pinos during my recent trip. The man was a son of Lorenzo de Ruvalcaba and Catalina González (Catalina Gallegos in the Pinos nuptial-Hernando Martel's seed?).  His brother, Joseph de Ruva
2 CONC lcaba, married Petra or Petronila Díaz.  The parents, Lorenzo and Catalina, were residents of Nochistlán, reason why the newlyweds had their first child christened there.
2 CONT 	Lorenzo de Ruvalcaba was a son of Francisco González de Ruvalcaba y López de Fuenllana, dead in Mexico City before Beatriz López de Fuenllana, his mother, made her will in Teocaltiche in 1607.  Francisco married Ana de la Paz,
2 CONC  but said will says he left one legitimate son and three bastard sons.  I know not which of the two was Lorenzo.
2 CONT 	The Pinos wedding: 15 Sep 1658-"Juan de Ruvalcaba, vecino de Teocaltiche, hijo legítimo de Lorenzo de Ruvalcaba y Catalina Gallegos, con Catalina de Sena, vecina de Zacatecas, hija legítima de Pedro de Herrera y Leonor Ortiz."
2 CONT 	The Nochistlán christening: 28 July 1659: "Nicolás, hijo de Juan de Ruvalcaba y Catalina de Sena su mujer vecinos del valle de Nochistlán.  Fue la madrina Agueda de Ruvalcaba, viuda."
2 CONT 	The widowed godmother was Juan's sister.  She married Diego de Arellano.  Their daughter, Catalina de Arellano married in Teocaltiche 25 Aug 1667 to Diego Jiménez.
2 CONT 	Juan and Catalina de Sena did not remain in Nochistlán.  They set up shop in Teocaltiche, of which he was a "vecino" when he wed in Sierra de Pinos.
2 CONT
2 CONT .Look for the MD of 10 December 1735 (6120, AGN) sent previously, where Lorenzo de Ruvalcaba (married to Catalina González-residents of Nochistlán) and Josepha Bautista de Ruvalcaba are sibs.  They're the two natural offspring o
2 CONC f Francisco de Ruvalcaba that I've found
