1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wedding [1]
2 CONT In the town of Aguascalientes on the ninth day of the month of July of one thousand six hundred and seventy years, I married and veiled, in facie ecclesiae , Antonio Díaz [de Lomas], neighbor of this town, legitimate son of Don Ju
2 CONC an [Francisco] Díaz de Lomas and of Ángela de Mérida [y Miranda], residents of the City of Zacatecas, with Luisa de los Reyes , legitimate daughter of Luis de los Reyes and Juana Tiscareño, having preceded all the proceedings esta
2 CONC blished by the Holy Council of Trent, having read the admonitions on three holidays that were Sunday, June 29, St. Peter's Day, and July 2, Visitation Day, and Sunday, July 6 of this year, and this did not result in an impediment;
2 CONC  Ensign Juan de Castro, Álvaro Marín de Peñaloza and Andrés Muñoz were witnesses. And for the record I signed it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dⁿ Baltazar Fernando de Castilla
2 CONT Death [2]
2 CONT In the town of Aguascalientes on the fourteenth day of the month of September of [one thousand six hundred] ninety years in her parish I buried Luisa de los Reyes , a Spanish woman, wife of Antonio Dias, she confessed and received
2 CONC  the holy sacraments, viaticum and extreme unction. She did not make a will because she did not have assets and for the record I signed it above .
2 CONT
2 CONT Dⁿ Baltassar Fernando Altamirano of Castilla
