1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of Diego Delgado and Juana Díaz, he was baptized on March 30, 1613 in the parish of Sierra de Pinos, his godfather being Francisco de Cardona [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wedding [2]
2 CONT Joseph Delgado and Francisca Gabadi, were married
2 CONT
2 CONT In the town of Aguascalientes, on thirty days of the month of August of one thousand six hundred and forty-four years, having preceded the provisions of the Holy Council of Trent and the admonitions Sunday twenty-one, twenty-four 
2 CONC day of the Lord Bartholomew the Apostle, Sunday twenty-eighth of said month and year, I married and gilded Joseph Delgado, a native of Sierra de Pinos, son of Diego Delgado and Juana Dias, with permission from his parish priest; w
2 CONC ith Francisca Gabadi, a native of this jurisdiction, legitimate daughter of Luis de Tiscareño and Lorenza Ruiz de Esparsa. His godfathers were Lope Ruiz de Esparsa and Francisca Gabadi , his grandparents, and witnesses to the wedd
2 CONC ing were Diego Delgado, Domingo de Laris, and Gaspar de Palos . And for the record, I signed it above
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Diego de Torres y Rivera
2 CONT Will (partial) [3]
2 CONT [18 March 1684]
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God almighty amen. May as many as I see this letter, Joseph Delgado, a native of the Sierra de Pinos jurisdiction of this Kingdom of [New] Galicia, legitimate son of Diego Delgado and Juana Díaz, his legitimate wife
2 CONC , my deceased parents. Neighbors who were from said jurisdiction of Sierra de Pinos. As being...
2 CONT
2 CONT Yten declare that Juan Delgado, my brother, a resident of Sierra de Pinos, is indebted to me for more than forty pesos. I order that he declare it, the aforementioned being be charged.
2 CONT
2 CONT And I declare that I am married and veiled according to the order of Our Holy Mother Church with Francisca Gabai, my wife. And <? > at the time and when I contracted said marriage I had and carried as capital two hundred pesos in 
2 CONC cows and mares, with another slave named Luisa, a dark mulatto, who was a little more or less six years old when I inherited her from Juana Díaz, my mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT And I declare that at the time and when I contracted said marriage with the said Francisca Gabai, my wife, she received in dowry from the hand of Luis de Tiscareño and Lorenza Ruiz de Esparza, parents of the said my wife, my lords
2 CONC  and in-laws, one thousand ninety-one pesos in the goods that for said dowry letter…
2 CONT
2 CONT Yten declare that during our marriage we have had and procreated by our legitimate children and heirs Juan, Luis, Joseph, Diego, Lorenza, Maria, Teresa, Elvira and Sebastiana. All over twenty-five years old, except Sebastiana Delg
2 CONC ado, maid.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death [4]
2 CONT Joseph Delgado, husband of Francisca Gabaii
2 CONT
2 CONT In the town of Aguascalientes on the fourth of July, year one thousand six hundred and eighty-five, in the parish church I buried Joseph Delgado, a Spaniard, resident of this jurisdiction, husband of Francisca Gavaii. He confessed
2 CONC , received the viaticum and the sacrament of extreme unction, made a will before Don Alonso Nabarreta, public notary, ordered that a mass be sung for him in person, ordered that a novena of recited masses be said to him, ordered t
2 CONC hat they be given to the brotherhood of the Sacramento sanctuary fifteen ducats of Castile and that the forced orders be paid, he leaves no other pious work, he leaves his wife, Francisca Gabaii, and his son Luis Delgado for his e
2 CONC xecutors. And for the record, I signed it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Balthassar Fernando Altamirano of Castile
2 CONT Fuentes
