1 NAME Ana María /Gómez Robledo/
2 GIVN Ana María
2 SURN Gómez Robledo
2 _MARNM Gómez Robledo
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1630
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santa Fe
3 STAE Provincia de Nuevo México
3 CTRY Reino de Nueva España
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ana Maria Gómez Robledo''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no evidence that Ana was married or had any children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ana Gómez Robledo is the daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Francisco-Gomez/6000000001660241143?through=6000000013095380674 Francisco Gómez] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Ana-Robledo-Romero/6000000005024488005?through=60000
2 CONC 00001660241143 Ana Robledo Romero]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Ana is said to have been taken captive and held at Taos, during the Revolt of 1680, where she died in captivity, date uncertain.  However, she appeared on the Don Diego de Vargas census 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693 in El Paso del Nor
2 CONC te, Nuevo México. Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seventh household, nine sisters and nieces, four dependents
2 CONT
2 CONT Sgto. major Bartolomé Gómez Robledo, unmarried, states that he has the following persons as family: doña Juana Ortiz, widow, his sister; doña '''Ana Maria Robledo'''; doña Maria Ortiz; Francisca Lucia; Maria Rosa; doña Ana Gómez; 
2 CONC Gregoria; Francisca; and four female and two male dependents, named Magdalena, Petrona, Maria, and Ana; and Luis and Sebastian.  He states that he will enter with me, the governor and captain general, solely to establish his house
2 CONC hold and sow his fields and after this is done, he will come and enter with all the persons mentioned.
2 CONT
2 CONT To The Royal Crown Restored, pg. 40
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Kessell, John L. and Hendricks, Rick, editors, To The Crown Restored, The Journals of Don Diego de Vargas, New Mexico, 1692-1694, University of New Mexico Press. 1995, ISBN 0-8263-1559-3
2 CONT --------------------
