1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marriage to Luisa de los Reyes [1]
2 CONT In the town of Aguascalientes on the ninth day of the month of July of one thousand six hundred and seventy years, I married and veiled, in facie ecclesiae , Antonio Díaz [de Lomas] , resident of this town, legitimate son of Don J
2 CONC uan [Francisco] Díaz de Lomas and of Ángela de Mérida [y Miranda], residents of the City of Zacatecas, with Luisa de los Reyes, legitimate daughter of Luis de los Reyes and Juana Tiscareño, having preceded all the proceedings esta
2 CONC blished by the Holy Council of Trent, having read the admonitions on three holidays that were Sunday, June 29, St. Peter's Day, and July 2, Visitation Day, and Sunday, July 6 of this year, and this did not result in an impediment;
2 CONC  Ensign Juan de Castro, Álvaro Marín de Peñaloza and Andrés Muñoz were witnesses. And for the record I signed it.
2 CONT
2 CONT D. Baltazar Fernando de Castilla
2 CONT Marriage to Rosa María de Molina [2]
2 CONT In the town of Aguascalientes on the twentieth day of the month of April of [one thousand six hundred] ninety-four years, I married and veiled, in facie ecclesiae , Antonio Dias de Lomas , a Spaniard, resident of this said town, w
2 CONC idower of Luisa de Tiscareño, with Rosa Maria de Molina, Spanish, neighbor of this said town, legitimate daughter of Christobal de Molina and Cathalina Saldana, deceased. Having preceded the procedures established by the Holy Coun
2 CONC cil of Trent. And three banns were read on three holidays inter missarum solemnia, the first Sunday the eleventh, the second Monday the twelfth and the third Tuesday the thirteenth of the said month of April, Easter days. And when
2 CONC  expressing his wishes, Don Francisco Tello de Lomas, Antonio Ruiz Escamilla and Antonio Alvares were witnesses. And for the record I signed it.
