1 NOTE {geni:about_me} May 4, 1694: Jorje Jaimes, Spanish, native and resident of this town [Aguascalientes], son of unknown parents, I appear before your worship and say that to better serve God our Lord I have a treaty and agreement to
2 CONC  contract a marriage according to order of Our Holy Mother Church with Maria Delgado , Spanish [she said she was twenty years old], neighbor and native of this town, legitimate daughter of Juan Delgado and Margarita Lopez de Lisal
2 CONC di... [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wedding [2]
2 CONT Jorge Xaimes, Spanish, with Maria Delgado married and veiled
2 CONT
2 CONT In the town of Aguascalientes on May twenty-third of [one thousand six hundred] ninety-four years, I married and veiled in facie ecclesie Jorge Xaimes, a Spaniard, neighbor and native of this town [Aguascalientes], son of unknown 
2 CONC parents with Maria Delgado , neighbor and native of this town, legitimate daughter of Juan Delgado and Margarita Lopes de Lisaldi. Having preceded the proceedings ordered by the Holy Council of Trent. And [the] three admonitions w
2 CONC ere read on three holidays inter missarum solemnia , the first Sunday the ninth and the second Sunday the sixteenth and Thursday the twentieth of the said month of May, the day of the Lord's ascension. And when expressing his wish
2 CONC es, Lorenço de Arismendi, Antonio Sagredo, and Joseph de la Cruz were witnesses. And for the record I signed it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fuentes
